Copy the .ascii files into your application ascii/cat_ascii directory and
gmake from ascii.

Copy edb.def and the .sym files to your application capfast directory.

Copy the .c files to your application src directory.


OMS58 support has been removed because it seemed to be causing trouble.
Anyone who needs it will have to do their own experimenting.

The edb.def file lacks support for the mbbiDirect record which is probably
an oversight on the part of Gemini (an embbid symbol is available in the
Gemini distribution).

None of this has been tested (by me) with interrupts.  The function omsSetup
needs to be called prior to iocInit to initialize certain parameters and it
is here that interrupt operation would be defined.  The following are
extracts from the VxWorks startup script for the Michelle Cryostat Control
System.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Load any application records, device support or drivers here,
# or code for subroutine records
ld < ./bin/mv167/drvOms.o
ld < ./bin/mv167/devOms.o
ld < ./bin/mv167/recMotor.o

ld < ./bin/mv167/amslib.o
ld < ./bin/mv167/elglib.o
ld < ./bin/mv167/etnetio.o
ld < ./bin/mv167/crulib.o
ld < ./bin/mv167/ccsStartup.o

ld < epics/extensions/bin/mv167/pvload

...................

omsSetup(2,8,0xFC00,0,1,6)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The omsSetup call indicates that the rack contains 2 OMS cards with 8 drive
channels, with the default base addresses, no interrupts, dummy interrupt
level (1) and a polling rate of 10 Hz (60/6).


Len Lawrence (lcl@roe.ac.uk)

1997 Aug 19






